Key decisions pinned in the plan:

- **Config**: `WAV_MAX_FILE_MB` env var via `envSchema` (ADR-005), `z.coerce.number().int().positive().default(500)`, documented in `.env.example`.
- **Rotation semantics**: `WavRecorderOptions.maxBytes` bounds on-disk size per part (header included); writes split at `blockAlign` boundaries so every file stays `<= maxBytes` with no split samples; rotation finalizes the current part before opening the next, all serialized on the existing write queue.
- **Naming**: part 1 stays `<stem>.wav` (ADR-007 bundle contract preserved); rotations produce `<stem>.part-002.wav`, `.part-003.wav`, ... opened with `wx`.
- **Test seam**: `SessionManagerDeps.wavMaxBytes` resolved lazily in `start()` so `app.test.ts` can inject byte-scale caps; unit tests exercise `maxBytes` directly.
- **Assumptions in Risks**: multi-part sessions extend the three-file ADR-007 bundle additively (part-001 naming rejected as it would rename the pinned `<stem>.wav`); Review playback serves part 1 only (flagged as follow-up); MiB unit confirmed.

